I was under the impression that your _maximum_ visited
dungeon level (not your actual level) would define how
tough monsters are generated.

> No, I'm pointing out that "keep XL low" is a
> frequent recommendation here from those successful
> ascenders.

In this generality, even though there's nothing expressed
to stay at XL:1, I wouldn't agree.

When and how do I increase XL?
- wraiths, they appear in the mid game, at that time I
    even reprieve wraiths to kill them later when I can
    get a more advantageous XL gain (i.e. immediately
    after a regular XL gain through monster kills)
- foocubi, I don't get involved with those
- potions, I save them to become admitted for the quest,
    drink them (as with wraiths) when the gain will be at
    max (though I drink them rarely post quest (only if
    I am    in need of a skill slot), because they serve
    as escape means for the late game, and also as part
    of a alchemic recipe those potions are very helpful)
- killing monsters, yes, I kill them immediately; they
    provide food, occasionally resistancies, and the HPs
    that come with the level gains are necessary as an
    additional buffer to survive.

And when do I not increase XL?
- if I've found a temple to donate and a bit money is
    missing I avoid killing monsters if it would level
    me up.

If I need skill slots I deviate from the above procedures
as necessary.

